-------------------------- MODULE MCRNResendTiming --------------------------
(***************************************************************************)
(* The instances of RNResendTiming.  MCRNResendTiming.cfg is the code's    *)
(* rule at the defaults with one tick of 500 ms: resend delay initial and  *)
(* maximum 2000 ms (4), the minimum rounded up to one tick (1),            *)
(* reliable_message_timeout 10 s (20), no back-off.                        *)
(* MCRNResendTimingBrokenBackoff.cfg is the first version's schedule with  *)
(* one tick of 100 ms: resend delay initial 1000 ms (10), maximum 2000 ms  *)
(* (20) and back-off to 8.  It must fail AttemptsBeforeTimeout: a sample   *)
(* sets rto to 1.5 s at the first tick, and the sends at 0, 1.5 and 4.5 s  *)
(* are all that fit before the timeout at 10 s, three where four are       *)
(* owed.  It passes ConfigAccepted, so the validation rule alone does not  *)
(* keep the property; it needs the delay without back-off.                 *)
(* MCRNResendTimingSeeded.cfg is the seeded start at the current defaults  *)
(* (2 s initial and maximum delay, the transport's round trip reported at  *)
(* 200 ms giving a 300 ms delay) and MCRNResendTimingBrokenUnseeded.cfg    *)
(* its reversed witness, the transport's round trip ignored: it must fail  *)
(* SeededGapBounded.  MCRNResendTimingRefused.cfg lets a first send be     *)
(* refused for 9 s and MCRNResendTimingBrokenRefusedClock.cfg is its       *)
(* reversed witness, the refusal starting the clock: it must fail          *)
(* AttemptsBeforeTimeout.  MCRNResendTimingPaced.cfg is the paced walk     *)
(* with one packet an update for the one record on the wire and a block    *)
(* whose first pass outlasts the timeout (the product's default is 256    *)
(* calls an update of one packet each, paced by the send budget), and      *)
(* MCRNResendTimingPacedSmall.cfg the same with the small record and two   *)
(* packets an update; their reversed witnesses                             *)
(* MCRNResendTimingBrokenUnsentFirst.cfg and                               *)
(* MCRNResendTimingBrokenUnsentFirstHeld.cfg walk the never-sent numbers   *)
(* first and must fail AttemptsBeforeTimeout and NoDueRecordHeld.          *)
(* MCRNResendTimingPacedSmallRoomOne.cfg is the recorded limit: two due    *)
(* records and one packet an update must fail NoDueRecordHeld, in the      *)
(* model as in the code.  MCRNResendTimingPacedRefused.cfg lets the        *)
(* transport refuse any packet carrying a record on the wire and checks    *)
(* RetryPlanned; its reversed witness                                      *)
(* MCRNResendTimingBrokenRefusedOffWire.cfg puts a refused resend back     *)
(* among the never-sent numbers and must fail it.                          *)
(* MCRNResendTimingFilterSparse.cfg is the RTT filter on a sparse sender   *)
(* (the previous message acked before the record's first send, nothing in *)
(* flight since) and MCRNResendTimingBrokenSilenceOnGap.cfg its reversed  *)
(* witness, any 1 s gap between acks a silence: it must fail               *)
(* RefuseOnlyAfterOwedSilence.                                             *)
(***************************************************************************)
EXTENDS RNResendTiming
=============================================================================
